--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY CONTENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The palettes in inst/extdata/palettes/ are content rather than code. Each states
its own terms in its `meta.license` field, and where a licence requires a
citation, in `meta.attribution`. This file summarises them; the palette files
are authoritative.

  carriers            energypal's own colours, following IEA World Energy
  technologies        Outlook conventions. Not reproduced from any published
                      figure. Taxonomy branches cite their classification
                      source individually as `_taxonomy_source`.

  owid                Colours approximated from Our World in Data charts.
                      CC BY 4.0 - attribution required.
                      https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

  eia, epa            Colours approximated from US federal agency figures.
                      Public domain (17 U.S.C. 105).

  ipcc                Colours approximated from IPCC AR6 WGIII Ch.3 Fig 3.8.
                      IPCC material may be reproduced with acknowledgement.

  windatlas_speed     Approximated after the Global Wind Atlas.
                      CC BY 4.0 IGO - attribution required, and the GWA terms
                      add a mandatory and binding condition: cite The World Bank
                      as the data provider and reference ESMAP as the source of
                      funding. Creative Commons ported the IGO variant at 3.0
                      only, so the operative deed text is CC BY 4.0.
                      https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

  solaratlas_ghi      Extracted from Global Solar Atlas poster maps.
  solaratlas_pvout    CC BY 4.0 - attribution required. The GSA terms add a
                      WIPO/UNCITRAL dispute-resolution clause.
                      https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The bundled dataset owid_energy_mix is from Our World in Data, CC BY 4.0.

